# Vendored third-party sources are kept BYTE-IDENTICAL to their upstream
# release. That is the point of vendoring: a patched copy of an audited library
# is an unaudited library, and the recorded SHA-256 digests in
# assets/vendor/nostr-crypto/PROVENANCE.md only mean something if nothing here
# has been reformatted.
#
# Upstream ships a few lines with trailing whitespace. Stripping them would be a
# silent local modification, so `git diff --check` is told not to police these
# paths. `tools/nostr-crypto.test.mjs` asserts every vendored file against its
# recorded digest, which is a stronger guarantee than a whitespace check.
assets/vendor/** -whitespace
